+## Versioned internal review companion
+
+`internal-review-launch/v1` is a proposed additive contract, not an active route
+merely because its document is published. Only after explicit owner ratification
+and separately scoped bootstrap/installation approval may its exact
+`operator-developer-cortex-memory` initial L2 plan-review use-case use a controlled
+Pi SDK child instead of the CLI. No builder, G6, other goal/lane/provider or data
+scope is covered; ordinary dispatch and every legacy/public-v1 refusal remain.
+
+The companion's trusted authority port and host-side admission gate must verify
+its single-use permit, exact model pair, native reasoning, scoped account/data
+policy, isolation, executed identity and incremental-charge accounting before
+invoking Pi's installed Anthropic provider/auth. Pro/OAuth is owner-attested:
+model improvement and paid extra usage off; NO separate broker or auth repair.
+The owner-accepted subscription policy is purpose-bound, NOT ZDR; prepaid quota
+is separate from incremental dollar caps. Provider-use/native-runtime evidence
+remains required. It cannot authorize or accept itself, silently switch auth,
+model or reasoning, load unrelated resources, or reuse an old receipt as a permit.
+See `../docs/contracts/internal-review-launch-v1.md` and its explicit bootstrap
+amendment. Publication, a human offline check or fixture output is not runtime
+admission, an independent frontier review, or downstream execution authority.
